Tom: Let''s begin near the river. London is an ancient port city with a long history.
Emma: Great. Can we see Tower Bridge first? People say it''s a symbol of the city.
Tom: Of course. After that, we can visit the National Gallery to see the paintings.
Emma: Wonderful! But first I need to get my phone charged. The battery is almost dead.
Tom: No problem. There''s a café nearby where you can charge it.
Emma: Perfect. Then let''s keep our eyes open for the historic sites along the way.', 'Emma 和 Tom 商量在伦敦怎样开始一天;Tom 建议从河边开始,因为伦敦是历史悠久的古老港口城市;先去看作为城市象征的塔桥,再去国家美术馆看画;Emma 想先给手机充电,Tom 说附近咖啡馆可以充;然后一路留心历史古迹。', 'uk_female', '[{"q":"Where does Tom suggest starting their day?","type":"choice","answer":"A","options":["Near the river.","At the airport.","In a shopping mall.","Outside the city."]},{"q":"What does Tom say about London?","type":"choice","answer":"B","options":["It has no history.","It is an ancient port city.","It is a very small town.","It is far from the river."]},{"q":"What is Tower Bridge said to be?","type":"choice","answer":"A","options":["A symbol of the city.","A new railway station.","A modern art gallery.","A famous restaurant."]},{"q":"Why does Emma need to stop first?","type":"choice","answer":"B","options":["To buy a new map.","To get her phone charged.","To meet a friend.","To have lunch."]},{"q":"What will they do along the way?","type":"choice","answer":"C","options":["Sleep on a bench.","Look for a car park only.","Keep their eyes open for historic sites.","Avoid all old buildings."]}]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, 'long', 'required2', 'U4');
In the 16th century, Wales was joined to the Kingdom of England.
Later, Scotland and then Ireland were added.
In the 20th century, the southern part of Ireland broke away.
Today most people simply use the shortened name, the UK.', '许多人被英国的各种名字弄糊涂;16世纪威尔士并入英格兰王国;后来苏格兰、再后来爱尔兰也加入;20世纪爱尔兰南部脱离;如今大多数人就用简称 the UK。', 'uk_female', '[{"q":"What confuses many people?","type":"choice","answer":"D","options":["The weather in London.","The price of tickets.","The number of museums.","The different names for the UK."]},{"q":"Which country was joined to England in the 16th century?","type":"choice","answer":"A","options":["Wales.","Scotland.","France.","Ireland."]},{"q":"What happened in the 20th century?","type":"choice","answer":"B","options":["Wales joined England.","The south of Ireland broke away.","Scotland left the UK.","London was built."]},{"q":"What name do most people use today?","type":"choice","answer":"C","options":["Great England.","The Roman land.","The UK.","The Kingdom of Wales."]},{"q":"In what order were the countries added?","type":"choice","answer":"D","options":["Ireland, then Wales, then Scotland.","Scotland, then Ireland, then Wales.","France, then Wales, then Scotland.","Wales, then Scotland, then Ireland."]}]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, 'short', 'required2', 'U4');
Jack: Yes, the pub is at the heart of village life. People come here to meet friends.
Lily: What should I try? I''d love to taste something traditional.
Jack: You must try the beef stew. And many people enjoy a glass of wine or a local beer.
Lily: That sounds lovely. Is there music too?
Jack: Yes, sometimes there''s traditional music and dancing in the evening.
Lily: How wonderful! It''s a great way to experience the local culture first-hand.', 'Lily 觉得乡村酒馆古老温馨,问这是否是当地传统;Jack 说酒馆是村庄生活的中心,人们来这儿见朋友;推荐 Lily 尝炖牛肉,还有人喝葡萄酒或本地啤酒;晚上有时有传统音乐和舞蹈;Lily 觉得这是亲身体验当地文化的好方式。', 'uk_female', '[{"q":"What does Jack say the pub is?","type":"choice","answer":"A","options":["At the heart of village life.","A brand-new building.","A place no one visits.","An empty old house."]},{"q":"What traditional food does Jack suggest trying?","type":"choice","answer":"B","options":["Fried rice.","Beef stew.","Cold pizza.","Sweet cakes."]},{"q":"What drinks do many people enjoy there?","type":"choice","answer":"C","options":["Only cold water.","Hot coffee only.","Wine or local beer.","Fruit juice only."]},{"q":"What sometimes happens in the evening?","type":"choice","answer":"D","options":["The pub closes early.","Everyone goes home.","No one speaks.","There is traditional music and dancing."]},{"q":"How does Lily feel about the pub?","type":"choice","answer":"A","options":["It''s a great way to experience local culture.","It is boring and cold.","It is too modern.","It has nothing to offer."]}]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, 'long', 'required2', 'U4');
The Romans came first and built many towns and roads.
Then the Anglo-Saxons introduced the beginnings of the English language.
The Vikings left behind new words and many place names.
Finally the Normans conquered England and changed the legal system.', '四群人在不同时期先后占领了英国;罗马人最先到来,修建了许多城镇和道路;接着盎格鲁-撒克逊人带来了英语的雏形;维京人留下了新词和许多地名;最后诺曼人征服了英格兰并改变了法律制度。', 'uk_female', '[{"q":"How many groups took over Britain?","type":"choice","answer":"B","options":["Two.","Four.","Six.","Ten."]},{"q":"What did the Romans build?","type":"choice","answer":"C","options":["Castles only.","A new flag.","Many towns and roads.","A football team."]},{"q":"What did the Vikings leave behind?","type":"choice","answer":"D","options":["Only castles.","A new legal system.","Roman roads.","New words and place names."]},{"q":"What did the Normans do?","type":"choice","answer":"A","options":["They conquered England and changed the law.","They left Britain at once.","They built no castles.","They spoke only English."]},{"q":"Who introduced the beginnings of English?","type":"choice","answer":"B","options":["The Romans.","The Anglo-Saxons.","The Vikings.","The Normans."]}]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, 'short', 'required2', 'U4');
Ben: Oh, I love Pingyao! Did you walk along Ming-Qing Street?
Anna: Of course, but I didn''t expect to see so many tourists there.
Ben: I know what you mean. But the snacks on that street are wonderful, aren''t they?
Anna: They really are. I also climbed the old city wall. It was like walking into history.
Ben: Did you visit the famous family courtyard as well?
Anna: Yes, but it wasn''t as big as I had expected. Still, the whole trip was great fun.', 'Anna 刚从平遥回来,觉得很棒;Ben 也爱平遥,问她有没有走明清街;Anna 走了,但没料到游客那么多;Ben 说那条街的小吃很棒;Anna 还爬了古城墙,像走进了历史;问她有没有去著名的家族庭院;去了,但没她想的那么大,不过整趟旅行很有趣。', 'uk_female', '[{"q":"Where has Anna just come back from?","type":"choice","answer":"C","options":["London.","Ireland.","Pingyao.","Scotland."]},{"q":"What surprised Anna on Ming-Qing Street?","type":"choice","answer":"D","options":["There were no shops.","It was completely empty.","It had closed down.","There were so many tourists."]},{"q":"What does Ben say is wonderful on that street?","type":"choice","answer":"A","options":["The snacks.","The tall buildings.","The quiet rooms.","The car park."]},{"q":"How did Anna feel on the old city wall?","type":"choice","answer":"B","options":["Bored and tired.","As if walking into history.","Cold and hungry.","Angry and lost."]},{"q":"What did Anna think of the family courtyard?","type":"choice","answer":"C","options":["It was the biggest she had seen.","It was completely closed.","It wasn''t as big as she had expected.","It had no rooms at all."]}]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, 'long', 'required2', 'U4');
People usually add a little milk to their tea.
They often eat small snacks such as cakes and sandwiches.
Friends greet each other warmly and sit down to chat.
It is a relaxing way to share time and keep an old custom alive.', '下午茶是许多英国家庭至今仍喜爱的古老传统;人们通常往茶里加一点牛奶;常配蛋糕、三明治等小点心;朋友们热情地相互问候、坐下闲聊;这是分享时光、让古老习俗延续下来的轻松方式。', 'uk_female', '[{"q":"What is afternoon tea?","type":"choice","answer":"D","options":["A new kind of sport.","A type of museum.","A famous castle.","An old British tradition."]},{"q":"What do people usually add to their tea?","type":"choice","answer":"A","options":["A little milk.","A lot of salt.","Cold water.","Hot oil."]},{"q":"What small snacks do people often eat?","type":"choice","answer":"B","options":["Only fruit.","Cakes and sandwiches.","Beef stew.","Rice and soup."]},{"q":"What do friends do at afternoon tea?","type":"choice","answer":"C","options":["They argue loudly.","They leave at once.","They greet each other and chat.","They stay silent."]},{"q":"Why is afternoon tea special, according to the passage?","type":"choice","answer":"D","options":["It costs a lot of money.","It is very tiring.","It ends all traditions.","It keeps an old custom alive."]}]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, 'short', 'required2', 'U4');

